{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAPoK5uQhZSTow6dPSgd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged` in `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`. It's the counterpart of `mark_changed`: it treats the current value as seen without borrowing it, so after calling it `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send.\n\nI added a test, `rx_mark_unchanged`, in `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`. It covers clearing a manual `mark_changed`, clearing a real `send`, and checks that the value is still readable afterwards. The test passes with the change and fails without it (it doesn't compile, since the method doesn't exist yet). `cargo fmt --check` is clean.\n\nI only ran the `rx_mark*` tests, not the full test suite, doc tests or clippy. Nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":33539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":270,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"408b063a-f763-4e52-a773-e38db9e5a8ee","uuid":"31501b0b-78c7-4cef-9998-6e356d73e5cf","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:14:17.228Z","request_id":"req_011CgAPoJqmUTafverKyfpnH"}
